[node name="Text" type="Label" parent="Credits/Content/Scroll" unique_id=1403998662]
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
text = "Cosy Village — art and music credits

Poly Haven materials, tree and sky: CC0 (https://polyhaven.com/license)
https://polyhaven.com/a/medieval_wood
https://polyhaven.com/a/roof_slates_02
https://polyhaven.com/a/plastered_stone_wall
https://polyhaven.com/a/medieval_blocks_03
https://polyhaven.com/a/forest_ground_04
https://polyhaven.com/a/tree_small_02
https://polyhaven.com/a/kloppenheim_06_puresky
Sky by Greg Zaal and Jarod Guest. Tree simplified for browser rendering.

Salamander Grand Piano: Alexander Holm, CC BY 3.0
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
Samples distributed by https://github.com/Tonejs/audio/tree/master/salamander
Locally served MP3 samples; original generative arrangements with pitch shifting,
filtering and reverb. Original sample README: audio/Salamander-LICENSE.txt

Village architecture, terrain, traveller and music arrangements: authored for Cosy.
Cobblestone texture: generated for this project using OpenAI ImageGen.
Arkenfall is a design reference; no Arkenfall assets were copied.

Representative-slice additions (2026-09-25):
Qwantani Sunset (Pure Sky), Greg Zaal (photography), Jarod Guest (processing).
CC0, https://polyhaven.com/a/qwantani_sunset_puresky
Original 1K HDR, locally served as textures/sunset.hdr.
Skinned traveller, woven textures, eight animation clips and willow geometry are
original scripted project artwork. Editable traveller source: assets/village/traveller.blend.
Footsteps, percussion, bass, birds and other new foley are original Web Audio synthesis.

2026-09-25 additions: original procedural cloud sky, stone arch bridge, ambient resident routes and bird geometry. Distant birch cards are rendered at runtime from the licensed birch model above; they add no third-party source asset.

2026-09-26 additions: original white smiling spirit, modeled in isolated Blender 5.2.1.
Editable source: assets/village/spirit.blend; generator: scripts/village/create_spirit.py.
Three PBR materials, no texture images or third-party character sources.
Genshin Impact and Arkenfall inform art direction; no assets from either game are used.
New palette, path shoulders, cottage details and spirit motion are original project work.

2026-09-26 fantasy village pass: original swept-roof cottage kit, painted CanvasTexture
surfaces, rounded tree geometry, vertex-painted mountain layers and suspended gardens.
Sources: features/village/architecture.ts, paintedTextures.ts, fantasyTrees.ts, world.ts.
Pastel blob residents reuse the original spirit mesh; accessories and animation are
original runtime geometry/transforms in life.ts. Older traveller/birch models and
photographic surfaces remain archived but are not loaded by the current village.

Recorded soundtrack and nature audio (2026-09-26)
------------------------------------------------
Quiet Village 1, 2, 3 and 4 — Holizna / HoliznaCC0.
Source: https://opengameart.org/content/quiet-village-collection
CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Full compositions retained; normalized and transcoded for local streaming.

Stream Sounds (stream1) — kurt.
Source: https://opengameart.org/content/stream-sounds
Creative Commons Attribution 3.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
Excerpt, mono downmix, normalization and MP3 transcode; overlapping loop boundaries.

Fireplace Sound loop — PagDev.
Source: https://opengameart.org/content/fireplace-sound-loop
Rain (loopable), sample 1 — Ylmir.
Source: https://opengameart.org/content/rain-loopable
Both CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Excerpts, mono downmix, normalization and MP3 transcodes; overlapping loop boundaries.

Detailed file provenance, duration and SHA-256: audio/recordings.json.
The village no longer schedules procedural musical notes or loads the Salamander
piano samples. Those earlier assets and credits are retained as historical sources.

Garden and pond kit (2026-09-27) — original project artwork.
17 models authored in Blender: flowers, sunflower, mint, vegetables, reeds,
lily, swan, duck, duckling, fish, watering can, basket, bread pouch and teapot.
Mint v2 adds original serrated green leaves and veins; bed signs and countdowns are authored in the runtime.
Editable source: assets/village/garden-pond.blend. Runtime: models/garden-pond.glb.
Named pivots are animated by the village runtime; no third-party models or textures.
Planting, watering, picking, pouring, bread crumbs, splashes and duck calls are
original procedural Web Audio effects. Existing recorded soundtrack credits above apply.

White dove and bird clearing (2026-09-27) — original project artwork.
Dove authored in Blender 5.2.1 LTS: assets/village/dove.blend;
runtime models/dove.glb; generator scripts/village/create_dove.py.
White plumage, scalloped wings, rosy cheeks and tiny peach feet use vertex colors.
Wren uses the original spirit with original flower/scarf/pouch accessories.
No third-party models or textures. The two-note coo is an original Web Audio effect.

Village puppies (2026-09-29) — original Cosy project artwork.
Mochi, Kiko, Biscuit and Cloud modeled in Blender 5.2.1 LTS.
Editable source: assets/village/puppies.blend; generator: scripts/village/create_puppies.py.
Runtime model: models/puppies.glb. No third-party character models or textures.

Puppy bark recordings — Brandon Morris (submitted by HaelDB).
Source: https://opengameart.org/content/dog-barking-mono
CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Four short cuts were trimmed, filtered, pitched and normalized for individual dogs.
The original recording is archived at assets/village/audio/dog-barking-source.wav;
file hashes and modifications are in docs/village/puppy-sound-manifest.json.

